        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-127578",
        ":question/problem": "$$\n\\displaystyle |\\begin{aligned}5 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}|=\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}5 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}| & =5\\cdot 7-(-9)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =35-27 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      }
